From c1fbc6effa87d724e77b9d25bdad05d38c5dbcc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:06:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat waits: answers by time and portable uid;
 the deadline trusts the card's comment probe

Review and adversarial pass of the previous head:
- _answered_since compared a park's --after-id and run integers, which are
  local to each board file: on the owner, a pool worker's park read an
  unrelated older comment as an answer, which disabled owner_fallback and the
  sweeper's 2 h escalation. It now counts comments created at or after the
  park event (synced created_at), and recognises the card's own worker by the
  portable writer_run_uid (writer_run_id only for unsynced rows).
- The 2 h deadline runs right after the card's own probe said "not yet", so it
  trusts that probe (escalate(trust_probe=True)): a worker-supplied filtered
  probe (--contains, --from-gateway) that misses the answer still escalates.
- The deadline applies only to a chat wait whose wake check is a wait-comment
  probe; one that named another producer (CI, a probe) may already be answered.

Tests: an old high-id comment is not an answer and a later one is; a filtered
probe that misses the answer escalates at 2 h; a CI-probe chat wait has no
deadline. 3 of 62 fail on the previous head; 29 neighbouring files (599 tests)
pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
